Flexbox is a powerful layout model for arranging items (horizontally or vertically) within a container, in a flexible and responsive way.
It is very helpful in arranging the elements perfectly and seamlessly. 
It has a number of properties to align the items in different ways horizontally or vertically.

Without flexbox we have to use CSS properties like margin, padding etc. which is difficult to precisely 
align items on the screen.

To enable flexbox styling on a container element we need to select it via CSS selectors and set display property to flex. 
For example: 
#parenr_container {
display:flex;
}
